# The runtime image needs only requirements.txt and TwitchChannelPointsMiner/; the
# `test` stage additionally needs requirements-dev.txt, tests/ and conftest.py (see
# Dockerfile). requirements-dev.txt is simply never excluded; tests/ and conftest.py
# are excluded above and re-admitted at the bottom. If you ever add a pattern that
# catches requirements-dev.txt, it needs re-admitting there too or the test stage
# stops building. Nothing the test stage uses reaches the published image -- the
# runtime stage does not COPY it.
# Named .dockerignore rather than .containerignore so docker and podman both honour it.

# Credentials and runtime state -- never send these to a builder.
cookies/
run.py
logs/
analytics/

# Local development
.venv/
.git/
.github/
.claude/
# `**/` is load-bearing: a bare `__pycache__/` matches only at the context root, so
# without it TwitchChannelPointsMiner/**/__pycache__ was copied into the published
# image. Harmless at runtime -- a mismatched magic number is just recompiled, and
# a matching one is still mtime-validated -- but it made a hand-built image differ
# from a CI-built one, which defeats the point of testing the image that ships.
# Keep the pattern even when host and image Python happen to agree.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
tests/
conftest.py

# Repo documentation and tooling
*.md
!README.md
.coderabbit.yaml
.pre-commit-config.yaml
.gitignore
assets/
scripts/
DELETE_PYCACHE.bat
pickle_view.py

# Re-admitted for the `test` stage only. These sit last because the final
# matching pattern wins, so they override the exclusions above.
!tests/
!conftest.py
# ...but `!tests/` re-admits everything under it, including the bytecode the
# `**/` patterns above exist to exclude, so re-exclude those. And the JS half
# runs in its own runner: node_modules must never be sent to a builder
# regardless of how it got back in.
tests/**/__pycache__/
tests/**/*.pyc
tests/js/node_modules/
